      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T20:28:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it might make more sense to define these as actual offsets i.e.:\n\n```\n#define CORE_CUR_FREQ 0x0\n#define CORE_SET_FREQ 0x4\n```\n\nThis way, if the size of the register space for a device changes, you just have to worry about encoding the new offset here, instead of having to change the multiplier to get to the next interface for each definition.\n\nand then use a per-cpu offset to hold the bases of each interface for each CPU. That way your accesses become (using read as an example)\n\n```\nreadl_relaxed(this_cpu_ptr(bases) + CORE_CUR_FREQ);\n```",
      "revId": "dd56e0941e95f103b5f200992d387113bc053d9e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
